   "text": "This SMILES is read from the drawing atom by atom. The stereochemistry is partly assigned from the standard VHL-ligand configuration rather than derived from the wedges alone.\n\n**Regions of the structure**\n- **Left end:** a 2-hydroxyphenyl group is attached to C3 of a pyridazine. The pyridazine ring is N\u2013N\u2013CH\u2013C\u2013CH\u2013C, and its C5 carries a para-substituted phenyl.\n- **Linker region:** the phenyl's para position bears an N-methylamino group. That nitrogen is attached to C4 of a piperidine. The piperidine nitrogen carries a CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013NH\u2013 unit.\n- **tert-Leucine unit:** the amide NH is bonded to a CH carrying a tert-butyl group, followed by C(=O).\n- **Hydroxyproline:** the tert-leucine carbonyl acylates the nitrogen of a 4-hydroxypyrrolidine. Its C2 carries a C(=O)NH amide.\n- **Right end:** the amide NH is attached to a CH(CH3) group on a para-substituted phenyl. That phenyl is bonded to C5 of a 4-methylthiazole.\n\n**Stereochemistry**\nI took the three stereocentres as the usual VHL-ligand configuration: (S)-tert-leucine, (2S,4R)-4-hydroxyproline and (S)-1-arylethylamine. I checked each chirality tag against the corresponding SMILES fragment in the VH032 ligand. The wedge directions in the image were not independently verified.\n\nSMILES: Oc1ccccc1-c1cc(cnn1)-c1ccc(cc1)N(C)C1CCN(CC1)CC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)(C)C)C(=O)N1C[C@H](O)C[C@H]1C(=O)N[C@@H](C)c1ccc(cc1)-c1scnc1C"
